      "evidence": [
        {
          "section": "abstract",
          "sentence": "We show two results supporting this conjecture: • First, we prove a conjecture of Oliveira that the first 𝑘 columns of Kac’s walk mix in time 𝑛𝑘 polylog(𝑛) uniformly in 𝑛 and 𝑘 ; • Secondly, we use this and a representation-theoretic argument to show that low-degree polynomials cannot distinguish Kac matrices from Haar matrices."
        },
        {
          "section": "body",
          "sentence": "The main ingredient in the proof of Theorem 2 is a proof that certain functions of Kac’s walk mix much more quickly than the walk itself."
